{"authored" [{"question" "q-282260" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $a=⟨2x,3,1⟩,$ $b=⟨-2x,0,4⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{280}.$ Then, in **ascending order**, the possible values of $x$ are\n\n$\\,x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039715/state.json" "file_sha256" "bf2af88b78c0f972594e3b8650f252763c7c3809d8ad4c0c602d226452cc8e27" "basis" 1376 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039715/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-282260" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2x & 3 & 1 \\\\ -2x & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2x & 1 \\\\ -2x & 4\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2x & 3 \\\\ -2x & 0\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(12-0)i-(8x+2x)j+(0+6x)k \\\\  & =⟨12,-10x,6x⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{{12}^{2}+(-10x)^{2}+(6x)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{144+100{x}^{2}+36{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{136{x}^{2}+144}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{280} \\\\ \\sqrt{136{x}^{2}+144} & =\\sqrt{280} \\\\ 136{x}^{2}+144 & =280 \\\\ 136{x}^{2} & =136 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the solutions are $x=-1,$ $x=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039715/state.json" "file_sha256" "bf2af88b78c0f972594e3b8650f252763c7c3809d8ad4c0c602d226452cc8e27" "basis" 1376 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039715/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-282260" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039715/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0118fa4be877af9d984d96913b8c4eb3649797d2aa3621bd31fccb9b4080a716" "basis" 1376 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039715/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-282260" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039715/state.json" "file_sha256" "bf2af88b78c0f972594e3b8650f252763c7c3809d8ad4c0c602d226452cc8e27" "basis" 1376 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039715/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-282260" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039715/state.json" "file_sha256" "bf2af88b78c0f972594e3b8650f252763c7c3809d8ad4c0c602d226452cc8e27" "basis" 1376 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039715/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-282260" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039715/state.json" "file_sha256" "bf2af88b78c0f972594e3b8650f252763c7c3809d8ad4c0c602d226452cc8e27" "basis" 1376 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039715/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-282260" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039715/state.json" "file_sha256" "bf2af88b78c0f972594e3b8650f252763c7c3809d8ad4c0c602d226452cc8e27" "basis" 1376 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039715/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-103552" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $a=⟨0,-2,3⟩,$ $b=⟨-2,1,-2x⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{53}.$ Find $x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042483/state.json" "file_sha256" "39e9640ddb6c31fdc5186e5c4d8a94ac5964a0ea3852df13abae427b92b301d8" "basis" 1548 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042483/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-103552" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -2x\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2x\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -2x\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(4x-3)i-(0+6)j+(0-4)k \\\\  & =⟨4x-3,-6,-4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{(4x-3)^{2}+(-6)^{2}+(-4)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16{x}^{2}-24x+9+36+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16{x}^{2}-24x+61}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{53} \\\\ \\sqrt{16{x}^{2}-24x+61} & =\\sqrt{53} \\\\ 16{x}^{2}-24x+61 & =53 \\\\ 16{x}^{2}-24x+8 & =0 \\\\ 2{x}^{2}-3x+1 & =0 \\\\ (2x-1)(x-1) & =0 \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2},\\,1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=\\frac{1}{2},\\,1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042483/state.json" "file_sha256" "39e9640ddb6c31fdc5186e5c4d8a94ac5964a0ea3852df13abae427b92b301d8" "basis" 1548 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042483/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-103552" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042483/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3a4d9f8db3082c207ca11e72800d17f68c2553d620fd2016dbb87908834d587f" "basis" 1548 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042483/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-103552" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042483/state.json" "file_sha256" "39e9640ddb6c31fdc5186e5c4d8a94ac5964a0ea3852df13abae427b92b301d8" "basis" 1548 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042483/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-103552" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "x=-1,\\,2"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042483/state.json" "file_sha256" "39e9640ddb6c31fdc5186e5c4d8a94ac5964a0ea3852df13abae427b92b301d8" "basis" 1548 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042483/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-103552" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "x=-2"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042483/state.json" "file_sha256" "39e9640ddb6c31fdc5186e5c4d8a94ac5964a0ea3852df13abae427b92b301d8" "basis" 1548 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/