pture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042784/state.json" "file_sha256" "25e8d57437c26b0e0f4a1e241cb3803cbc7be2053222c4644fd7af0690baed64"} {"question" "q-282260" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2x & 3 & 1 \\\\ -2x & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2x & 1 \\\\ -2x & 4\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2x & 3 \\\\ -2x & 0\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(12-0)i-(8x+2x)j+(0+6x)k \\\\  & =⟨12,-10x,6x⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{{12}^{2}+(-10x)^{2}+(6x)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{144+100{x}^{2}+36{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{136{x}^{2}+144}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{280} \\\\ \\sqrt{136{x}^{2}+144} & =\\sqrt{280} \\\\ 136{x}^{2}+144 & =280 \\\\ 136{x}^{2} & =136 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the solutions are $x=-1,$ $x=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042784/state.json" "file_sha256" "25e8d57437c26b0e0f4a1e241cb3803cbc7be2053222c4644fd7af0690baed64"} {"question" "q-282260" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042784/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1f9593abe2bcd968550617c130879f834c4232f5e69de9554b6a95fa36c71400"} {"question" "q-282260" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14